Two design conflicts stand out. The existing index checker reads the staging area or a commit, so its success cannot certify the current files. Also, CACHES.md forbids a session-start hook from opening cache files, so the hook cannot perform the same checks as a full report.

Several git-labelled requirements also need human judgement: history can show an edit, but it cannot establish whether that edit introduced a new decision or whether an uncommitted edit was lost.
