     1	# memory-check — vision
     2	
     3	A TypeScript tool that looks at a project, finds which memory it has, checks that memory against the two memory
     4	guidelines — `docs/memory-system/SOURCE_OF_TRUTH.md` (with `SOURCE_OF_TRUTH_REQUIREMENTS.yaml`) and
     5	`docs/memory-system/CACHES.md` — and tells the user what is there, what is missing and what is wrong: a full report on
     6	demand, and warnings at the start of a session.
     7	
     8	## Who it is for
     9	
    10	- **The project owner**, who wants to know, without reading the guidelines, whether a project's memory follows them.
    11	- **Every agent starting a session**, which must not start work on memory that is missing, stale or broken without
    12	  being told.
    13	
    14	## What it checks
    15	
    16	Only what the two guidelines require: each check is one requirement's `fails_if` (or **Fails if**) line, cited by its
    17	id. A requirement whose check is a reviewer's judgement is listed as needing a reviewer, never passed or failed by the
    18	tool. The tool adds no rule of its own.
    19	
    20	## What it will never do
    21	
    22	- Change any memory, entry, index or cache: it only reads, and writes only its own report.
    23	- Say a requirement passes without the evidence that shows it.
    24	- Load what the guidelines say is never loaded (another agent's transcripts, credentials, the whole memory tree at
    25	  once).
    26	- Replace `tools/memory_index.py`: where that tool checks a requirement, this one runs it and reports its result.
